var MFP_CONTEXT = '=== MIAMI FREEDOM PARK STADIUM — PROJECT KNOWLEDGE ===\n\nPROJECT OVERVIEW:\n  Name: Miami Freedom Park Stadium\n  Client: Miami Freedom Park LLC (Principals: Jorge Mas, Jose Mas)\n  Program: 25,000-seat MLS stadium for Inter Miami CF\n  Delivery: CM as Agent (Lemartec Corp)\n  Home Opener: April 4, 2026 — building open and operational\n  Phase: Post-Opening / Active Punch List Closeout\n  Level Up Role: Owner Representative\n\nTEAM:\n  Owner: Graham Oxley (day-to-day), Devon McCorkle, Victor Oliver (approvers)\n  CM/GC: Lemartec Corporation\n  AOR: Arquitectonica (ARQ)\n  Design Architect: MANICA Architecture\n  Cost Recovery: Kroll (target: $9M+ recoverable, delivery June 30)\n\nFINANCIALS:\n  Total Project Budget: $824,199,990\n  Budget at Closing: $710,953,041\n  Realized Changes: $93,987,589\n  Paid to Date: $412,731,063\n  Incurred to Date: $440,414,875\n  Past Due: $11,779,630\n  Stadium Base Contract: $530,448,817\n  Approved COs: $45,301,139\n  Committed to Date: $612,728,557\n  Stadium % Complete: 94.2% (base scope invoiced vs committed)\n  Lemartec Indirects Outstanding: $39,639,976\n  Retainage Held: $25,454,318\n\nTOP SUBCONTRACTORS (by CO volume):\n  Baker Concrete: 50 COs, $11.5M\n  A-1 All Florida: 46 COs, $9.1M\n  Qualico Steel: 50 COs, $3.8M\n  Glenn Rieder: 48 COs, $1.7M (carries 92% of punch items)\n\nACTIVE ISSUES:\n  1. HIGH: ARQ Payment Hold (~$1.5M Feb-Apr invoices)\n  2. HIGH: Kroll Cost Recovery Audit (delivery June 30, target $9M+)\n  3. HIGH: Punch List - Tile installation deficiency (disputed with Lemartec) - position: correction, not credit\n  4. HIGH: Punch List - Surface-mounted electrical conduit (spec required concealed) - position: correction, not credit\n  5. HIGH: HVAC Service Agreement - Hill York (urgent, pending signature)\n  6. HIGH: Lemartec Indirect Costs - $39.5M payment gap\n  7. HIGH: TCO / Certificate of Occupancy / Insurance\n  8. MEDIUM: Day 2 / Owner Requests - 60+ items in various stages\n  9. MEDIUM: Parker Company - Invoices 104 days past due\n\nKEY CONTRACTS:\n  Lemartec Trade Contract: 140-pg PDF\n  ARQ Agreement: Executed July 27, 2023 - Architect of Record\n  MANICA Agreement: Executed July 27, 2023 - Design Architect\n  Miller Electric: $28M outstanding\n\nPUNCH LIST: Active. Tile and conduit are main disputes with Lemartec. Position: correction, not credit.\nDAY 2 ITEMS: 60+ owner-directed post-opening items. Each needs scope definition, cost estimate, owner authorization. Distinct from punch list.\nCOST RECOVERY: Kroll engaged. Scope includes CO clawbacks, VE credits, OCIP, quantity verification, duplicate COs, defective work credits.';

